      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maintaining a Set\u003cCallback\u003e is tricky, as we want to avoid any strong references that would prevent the Binder death from being triggered in ConnectivityService.\n\nI\u0027ve updated ConnectivityDiagnosticsBinder to have a lock object for accessing the executor and synchronize on it here.\n\nAnother option is to return a NetworkRequest from the register call to ConnectivityService, and store it in a synchronized static collection (similar to how ConnectivityManager handles callbacks).\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1;l\u003d3598?q\u003dConnectivityManager\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject",
